window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"irelia","b":"locke","win":["Irelia","Irelia","Irelia","Irelia","Irelia","Irelia","Irelia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 2-3","text":"Step in when Ashen Pursuit (E) is spent — his only exit, 10s flat."},{"when":"Level 6","text":"Vanguard's Edge walls off his execute angle — his kill dream dies here."},{"when":"First item","text":"Buy anti-heal: Soul Ignition refunds the damage he takes, every 18s."},{"text":"Purgatory executes below a health threshold and runs 80 seconds at rank 3 — never take a sliver-HP fight inside the zone. Step out, top up, and force the duel once it is spent.","when":"2+ items"}],"wants":{"you":["Passive stacked before every trade","Q resets through the wave onto him","His burst walled out with R"],"foe":["Poke between your Q resets","One clean burst rotation","Escapes from your stacked all-ins"]},"early":"You out-trade him at every stage, starting level 1: Bladesurge resets through the wave keep you stuck to him, and his nails cost 70 mana a throw, so he pays for every poke. Don't count on Defiant Dance — his damage is magic and true, not physical. Force an exchange every time your passive is stacked; his kit wants clean burst windows and you never give him one.","mid":"Six through first item just adds locks to the cage — Vanguard's Edge cuts his angles and Flawless Duet stuns the engage. Ashen Pursuit is a flat 10 seconds and it is his engage AND his escape, so the window right after he spends it is the lane: dive it with your jungler. Buy Grievous Wounds before he refunds a lost trade through Soul Ignition.","late":"Two-plus items you are the reset duelist he can never cleanly kill — dashes keep you slippery, your R cuts his angles, and your scaling passes his outright. Split-push and dare him to answer, or group and dash through his frontline onto whoever matters most. This matchup is yours at all seven stages; play like it and close the game.","whys":["Level 1 is Irelia — Bladesurge resets off the wave keep you sticky and winning from the first trade.","Level 2 stays yours — stacked trades snowball on him, and every exchange compounds the lead.","Level 3 is Irelia: E-stun him mid-blink; Defiant Dance won't blunt magic.","Levels 4-5 favor you — Flawless Duet's stun punishes every engage he attempts.","Level 6 is Irelia because Vanguard's Edge walls off his execute angles entirely.","First item keeps you ahead — Grievous Wounds voids the heal Soul Ignition refunds.","2+ items stays Irelia — a reset duelist he can never cleanly kill just keeps scaling past him."]});
