window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"irelia","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Irelia","Irelia","Zaahen","Zaahen","Skill","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 2-3","text":"Reset trades plus the E stun window — bully him before his ult exists."},{"when":"Levels 4-5","text":"His ult hunts an Irelia with no reset targets — fight on live waves only."},{"when":"First item","text":"Full-stack Bladesurge DPS beats his sustain — the trades are yours again."},{"text":"Determination fills from every hit he lands on you: at full stacks he gains bonus Attack Damage and can revive, so a duel you already won can un-win itself. Disengage after the kill instead of standing over him.","when":"2+ items"}],"wants":{"you":["Trades with stacks and a live wave","E stuns on his commit windows","Extended fights at full stacks"],"foe":["You caught on a dead wave","Early-ult all-ins mid-cooldowns","Out-sustained unstacked trades"]},"early":"Hit him in the 2-3 window — Bladesurge resets and passive stacks out-trade him, and Flawless Duet's stun makes his answer arrive late every time. Then respect the shift at 4-5: his ult arrives early and punishes any Irelia caught without reset targets, so keep a live wave between you and never brawl on dead ground you cannot dash through.","mid":"Level 6 is an engagement-quality contest — your Vanguard's Edge against his ult, and the cleaner commit wins — but first item settles the argument: full-stack Bladesurge DPS out-trades his sustain in any real fight. Stack before you strike, stun his engage on reaction, and grind him down; your healing math now beats his outright.","late":"Two-plus items the duel is yours on repeat — reset mobility means he cannot pin you, the stun interrupts his all-in, and your sustained DPS outlasts everything he has left. Side-lane with waves to dance through, wall his disengage with R, and force the extended fight he keeps losing. Just never get caught minion-less — that is his only remaining win.","whys":["Level 1 is even — your Q resets are not truly online without wave setup yet.","Level 2 is Irelia's: Bladesurge resets and passive stacks out-trade him — force the exchange.","Level 3 stays yours — reset mobility plus the Flawless Duet stun owns the lane.","Levels 4-5 are his — the W pull and Aureate Rush dash catch you off the wave, and his Q heals him back every 6-10s.","Level 6 is his — Grim Deliverance heals him for a portion of its damage, so his all-in outlasts yours.","First item is a wash — your stacked DPS races his Q and R healing.","2+ items stays yours — reset mobility and the stun out-duel his all-in every time."]});
