window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"irelia","b":"masteryi","win":["Irelia","Irelia","Skill","Skill","Irelia","Master Yi","Master Yi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 1-2","text":"Reset tempo plus stacks bully his weak early — build the lead now."},{"when":"Level 6","text":"Stun cancels Meditate — burst him before Highlander's 85s answer."},{"when":"Enemy first item","text":"Wuju Style true damage ignores your armour — burst or don't fight."},{"text":"Highlander makes him immune to slows, so Vanguard's Edge only walls him — the stun is the part that still lands. Stun first and let your team collapse; never take the solo duel here.","when":"2+ items"}],"wants":{"you":["Snowballed early reset trades","A kill at 6 before his item","Short burst windows, never brawls"],"foe":["Safe farm through the lane","Every fight dragged long","Late crit duels you cannot match"]},"early":"Open aggressive — levels 1-2 your reset tempo and passive stacks bully his weak early, so trade every wave. Levels 3-5 tighten into a stun-reads contest: land Flawless Duet and trades stay yours, whiff and Wuju Style true damage answers. Never throw the stun into Alpha Strike — he is untargetable through it, and his attacks shorten its cooldown below 20s.","mid":"Level 6 is your kill window and you should force it — the E stun cancels Meditate, so his 10-second heal is wasted every time you hold the stun for it. Cash the window hard, because first item flips the lane: lifesteal plus true damage wins anything long, and Grievous Wounds keeps Meditate honest. From then on, burst only — stack, stun, unload, disengage.","late":"Two-plus items his crit DPS out-scales your skirmisher kit, so stop meeting him head-on. Play picks instead: dash through waves onto his carries, and stun him the instant Alpha Strike ends so your team's CC chains on. Don't expect Vanguard's Edge to kite him — Highlander makes him slow-immune, so the wall only blocks. Alone he out-duels you; grouped, your stun makes him everyone's problem.","whys":["Level 1 is Irelia — Bladesurge resets keep you stuck to him and winning the trade.","Level 2 stays yours: Q-reset tempo and passive stacking edge every exchange.","Level 3 evens out — your E cancels Meditate outright, but Alpha Strike goes untargetable through it.","Levels 4-5 stay a coin-flip around your E and Q resets — pure execution decides each trade.","Level 6 is Irelia's — Flawless Duet stuns him out of the burst, and Highlander is 85 seconds once he spends it.","First item is Yi's: lifesteal plus Wuju Style true damage wins long fights — armour will not save you.","2+ items stays Yi — full-crit DPS out-scales your skirmisher kit, so win with picks and your team."]});
